        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Illinois Institute of Technology, Boise State University, VanderCook College of Music, Episcopal Church\n- Places: United States\n- Topics: institutional history, founding, academic degrees, campus location\n\nFacts:\n- Illinois Institute of Technology traces its history to several 19th-century engineering and professional education institutions in the United States.\n- Boise State University was founded in 1932 by the Episcopal Church.\n- Boise State University became an independent junior college in 1934.\n- Boise State University has awarded baccalaureate and master's degrees since 1965.\n- VanderCook College of Music is located in a Mies van der Rohe building on the campus of Illinois Institute of Technology.",
